# Copy to .dev.vars for local development. Never commit real values.
# Wrangler loads only core's required secrets from it; deployment config
# (SIGN_IN, MODEL_GATEWAY) goes in with `wrangler dev --var`.
# No AI provider key goes here: model calls fail as "Connect an AI provider"
# until an admin (admin@acme.test locally) adds one in Settings, with a key
# of their own, which local connect seals with its TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY
# (apps/connect/.dev.vars).
# Shared with the router. `vp run dev` skips the router-secret check for
# requests to localhost, so it may stay empty locally.
ROUTER_SECRET=
# Signs session cookies and encrypts sign-in state. Any random value of at
# least 32 characters, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`. `vp run dev` signs
# people in through a local fake IdP (scripts/dev.ts): any email at
# acme.test, and admin@acme.test as an admin.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# Signs the capability each call to connect carries. The same value as in
# apps/connect/.dev.vars; at least 32 characters, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`.
CAPABILITY_SIGNING_KEY=
# Optional: Stephen's own Gmail mailbox, as a chat platform
# (src/channels/gmail.ts). Its door stays closed (404) until the first four
# are set. The audience, service account and subscription are the Pub/Sub
# push subscription's; the topic is the one the mailbox's watch publishes
# to. The mailbox's OAuth client and refresh token are connect's.
GMAIL_MAILBOX=
GMAIL_PUBSUB_AUDIENCE=
GMAIL_PUBSUB_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=
GMAIL_PUBSUB_SUBSCRIPTION=
GMAIL_PUBSUB_TOPIC=
